1
00:00:03,304 --> 00:00:12,767
Retail Lending
A home loan from the client's first call to disbursement — every hand-off, check and approval in one record.

2
00:00:12,772 --> 00:00:16,610
Kavita Ramchurn calls about a home loan
The loans executive logs the enquiry while on the phone

3
00:00:16,610 --> 00:00:33,738
Sign in as Sophie Lagesse — Loans Executive
Loans executive — takes the client’s call

4
00:00:33,738 --> 00:00:45,148
What she wants: a real-estate loan of MUR 4.5 million over 20 years

5
00:00:45,148 --> 00:00:52,954
Routing assigns lending enquiries round the loans team — this one stays with Sophie
The first-contact SLA clock starts now

6
00:00:52,954 --> 00:01:05,348
She qualifies on the call — drag the enquiry to Qualified, then Converted
Converting creates the client, the KYC case and the loan application

7
00:01:05,348 --> 00:01:08,070
The loan application is waiting in Retail Lending
Already at Pre-qualified, with the amount and tenure from the enquiry

8
00:01:08,070 --> 00:01:17,332
Application captured needs the client's income and the property value
The board refuses the move and says what is missing

9
00:01:17,332 --> 00:01:28,000
Open the record from the message and complete it
Purpose, income, existing repayments and property value

10
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:37,880
Tick the client's consent to the MCIB credit bureau check
No consent, no credit report

11
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:45,583
The CRM prices the loan and checks eligibility by itself
Genesis PLR + product margin = interest rate · monthly instalment · total interest

12
00:01:45,583 --> 00:01:52,549
Loan-to-value, debt-service ratio and eligibility
And the approval authority — up to MUR 5 million, the Loans Manager

13
00:01:52,549 --> 00:02:00,097
Now Application captured is accepted
The MCIB report is pulled and the client gets a status email

14
00:02:00,097 --> 00:02:11,938
Documents pending: the client is emailed the document checklist

15
00:02:11,938 --> 00:02:16,241
The Docs tab shows the checklist for a real-estate loan
What is in and what is still missing

16
00:02:16,241 --> 00:02:23,235
Send the client a secure upload link
No sign-in — she only sees the documents still needed

17
00:02:23,235 --> 00:02:29,542
Her uploads land on this application and tick off the checklist

18
00:02:29,542 --> 00:02:43,176
Documents in: Documents complete, then on to credit
Credit appraisal only accepts an eligible application — or one with its policy exceptions recorded

19
00:02:43,176 --> 00:02:47,256
The credit analyst picks up the application
Same record — another person, another form

20
00:02:47,256 --> 00:02:54,023
Sign in as Nadia Peerbux — Credit Analyst
Credit analyst — appraises the risk and recommends a decision

21
00:02:54,023 --> 00:03:00,975
The MCIB credit report is already on the application
Score, rating and reference came back from the credit bureau

22
00:03:00,976 --> 00:03:14,851
Switch to the Credit appraisal workbench form
Risk grade, recommendation and conditions

23
00:03:14,852 --> 00:03:23,243
Credit approval: the request goes to the right authority for the amount

24
00:03:23,243 --> 00:03:27,223
MUR 4.5 million: the Loans Manager decides
Four eyes — whoever sent it can never approve it

25
00:03:27,223 --> 00:03:34,405
Sign in as Rajiv Doorgakant — Manager, Loans & Fixed Income
Manager, Loans & Fixed Income — approves loans up to MUR 5 million

26
00:03:34,405 --> 00:03:54,525
Tools ▸ Approvals: grade, DSR, LTV and the analyst's recommendation on one card

27
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:59,393
Approved — the application moved itself to Offer issued
Decision, date and the PLR the offer is priced on are recorded

28
00:03:59,393 --> 00:04:05,021
The offer letter was generated and filed here
The client is emailed; an offer not accepted in 30 days lapses

29
00:04:05,021 --> 00:04:10,127
The client signs the offer — back to the loans executive
Record the signature, the security and the amount to disburse

30
00:04:10,127 --> 00:04:21,027
Sign in as Sophie Lagesse — Loans Executive
Loans executive

31
00:04:21,027 --> 00:04:51,785
Valuation, notary, fixed charge, life and building insurance

32
00:04:51,785 --> 00:05:02,923
Ready for disbursement needs perfected security and an approved KYC
Her KYC case is still open — the move is refused

33
00:05:02,923 --> 00:05:06,212
Finish the KYC case that was opened at conversion
Clients ▸ KYC & Compliance ▸ KYC Cases

34
00:05:06,212 --> 00:05:18,772
ID, proof of address and source of funds are on file
Tick the checks and the FATCA status

35
00:05:18,772 --> 00:05:30,969
Move it to Screening: sanctions and PEP lists are checked automatically
The result and its reference are written on the case

36
00:05:30,969 --> 00:05:37,540
Clear — Pending approval sends the case to Compliance
High-risk clients go to the MLRO instead

37
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:41,868
Compliance signs off the KYC case
Four eyes again: the loans executive cannot approve her own client

38
00:05:41,868 --> 00:05:48,027
Sign in as Fatima Hossenbux — Compliance Officer
Compliance officer — signs off KYC

39
00:05:48,027 --> 00:06:04,489
Tools ▸ Approvals: the KYC case with its risk score and rating

40
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:08,815
KYC approved — the loans executive tries again
Now the gate lets it through

41
00:06:08,815 --> 00:06:24,787
Sign in as Sophie Lagesse — Loans Executive
Loans executive

42
00:06:24,787 --> 00:06:29,748
An approval request goes to the operations checker
Maker-checker: whoever requests a disbursement cannot approve it

43
00:06:29,748 --> 00:06:37,517
Sign in as Ritesh Seewoo — Operations Checker
Operations checker — the second pair of eyes before money moves

44
00:06:37,517 --> 00:06:54,465
Tools ▸ Approvals: the disbursement request, with security and KYC status

45
00:06:54,465 --> 00:07:01,267
The loan is booked in the core loan system
The LMS account number is written back on the application

46
00:07:01,267 --> 00:07:05,312
The loans executive closes the application as Disbursed

47
00:07:05,312 --> 00:07:28,745
Sign in as Sophie Lagesse — Loans Executive
Loans executive

48
00:07:28,745 --> 00:07:34,067
Related: the new loan account, the KYC case and the insurance referral
Loan Servicing now follows instalments, arrears and the balance

49
00:07:34,067 --> 00:07:41,165
One record, the whole journey
Five people worked the same loan application — no re-keying, every step audited.
